# Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice  (Steam appid 814380)
#
# ✅ PLAYS (2026-08-25, first launch, no iteration): graphics, sound and
# controller all working. The first title here chosen for its INPUT
# requirements rather than its renderer -- it is the game the controller work
# was for -- and the first From Software / action title, so the first that
# needs input to be correct frame-by-frame rather than merely present.
#
# Measured DURING STARTUP AND LOADING, not during play (the process was gone
# before a gameplay sample was taken): ~300-425% CPU, 3:05 of CPU time in 90 s
# wall, one busy thread at 92.5% in the realtime band (R) with the main thread
# mostly idle -- the same healthy signature as Iron Nest and Chimera Squad, and
# the exact opposite of the "idling at 0-1% at a capability check" failure that
# a missing D3D11 backend produces.
#
# Verified from the live process that the per-app key really took, rather than
# assuming it from the registry:
#   prefixes/steam-winecx/.../system32/d3d11.dll   (DXMT, not builtin wined3d)
#   prefixes/steam-winecx/.../system32/dxgi.dll    (DXMT)
#   runtimes/.../winemetal.dll + winemetal.so      (both halves of the unixlib)
#
#   engine        proprietary (From Software)
#   exe           sekiro.exe -- PE32+ x86_64, no launcher, single exe in the tree
#   graphics      Direct3D 11 (imports d3d11.dll, dxgi.dll; also d3d9.dll)
#   input         XINPUT1_3.dll and DINPUT8.dll -- both imported
#   anti-cheat    none (checked for EasyAntiCheat/BattlEye/Denuvo/VMProtect/
#                 Arxan by name; zero hits, and no anti-cheat files on disk)
#   redist        d3dx11_43 and d3dcompiler_43 -- both already builtin in the
#                 runtime and present in the prefix, so no winetricks needed
#   size          15 GB
#
# ⚠️ No steam_appid.txt ships with this game, so a *-direct.env debug profile
# will NOT work as-is: sekiro.exe would re-launch itself via steam://run/814380
# and exit 53. Write one containing 814380 into the game directory first.
# See docs/RUNTIME.md section 9.

RUNTIME="winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64"
PREFIX="steam-winecx"

# D3D11, so wined3d cannot run it at all on this platform -- MoltenVK has no
# geometryShader, the adapter caps at feature level 9_3, and D3D11CreateDevice
# fails with 0x80004005. See docs/RUNTIME.md section 10.
#
# ⚠️ AND THIS LINE ALONE DOES NOT SELECT THE BACKEND for a Steam game -- BACKEND=
# exports WINEDLLOVERRIDES, which does not survive the Steam client hand-off.
# The per-application registry key does the real work, and was registered with:
#
#   bin/backend-install dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse steam-winecx \
#       winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64 --app 'sekiro.exe' --app-only
#
# There is no launcher here, so the usual trap (keying the override on the
# launcher rather than on the exe that creates the D3D device) cannot bite --
# sekiro.exe is the only executable in the tree.
BACKEND="dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse"

EXE='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steam.exe'
WORKDIR="$PREFIXES_DIR/steam-winecx/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam"

ARGS="-applaunch 814380"

PROFILE_ENV=(
    "WINEDEBUG=${WINEDEBUG--all}"
)

WINEDLLOVERRIDES=""
